WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.320
You might have seen the Matrix, but&nbsp;
can you explain the sixth cycle of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:09.200
humanity’s enslavement by the machines? We&nbsp;
couldn’t either till we made this guide!

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.960
In the aftermath of the lengthy Machine&nbsp;
War, A.I has conquered humanity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:20.240
but they've also become dependent on human's heat&nbsp;
and bioelectricity as a renewable energy source.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.280
A program called the Architect is assigned&nbsp;
to create a simulated reality called&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.320
the Matrix to imprison human minds&nbsp;
and keep their bodies healthy.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:36.000
The Architect first develops a simulated paradise,&nbsp;
but the humans discover it's fabricated and&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.040
reject it — to their death. A more&nbsp;
realistic simulation is then created,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:45.920
based on Earth's real history, and set at&nbsp;
humanity's "peak" in the late 20th century.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.280
However, prisoners still don't properly acclimate.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:57.200
Enter the Oracle — a new "intuitive" program that&nbsp;
analyzes human behavior. The Oracle theorizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.800
that humans may be more likely to accept the&nbsp;
Matrix's reality if given a choice, even a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:09.120
subconscious one. This function leads to nearly&nbsp;
99% of all subjects accepting the simulation.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:16.000
This update stabilizes the Matrix for 100 years,&nbsp;
but the collective disbelief of the remaining 1-2%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:24.000
of human minds has the potential to erode the&nbsp;
consensus reality and kill everyone inside. To&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:29.120
navigate this issue, the Matrix compiles the&nbsp;
anomalies caused by disbelievers until they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:34.400
reach a critical mass, then dumps them all&nbsp;
into a single, randomly-selected human mind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.840
This individual would have unparalleled&nbsp;
control over the reality of the Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.240
but the machines have a plan to deal with them.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:49.840
A hundred years after the birth of the first&nbsp;
stable Matrix, a human is born who recognizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:55.040
they live in a simulation. This person is&nbsp;
able to manipulate the simulation at will.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:00.640
This individual frees minds from the Matrix,&nbsp;
and forms a resistance against the machines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:06.080
in the real world. The freed humans build&nbsp;
the underground city of Zion and call their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:11.360
liberator "The One." What they don't know is&nbsp;
that without the reintegration of the extra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:17.200
code that resides within the One, the Matrix will&nbsp;
collapse, killing the majority of the human race.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:23.120
As a remedy, the Oracle manifests inside&nbsp;
the Matrix and positions herself as an ally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:28.240
who can use her gift of foresight to help&nbsp;
the One free humanity and end the Machine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:34.960
War. The Oracle leads the One to the Architect,&nbsp;
who offers them a grim choice — either reinsert&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:41.040
the extra code they carry into the Source and&nbsp;
allow the Matrix to reboot safely, or refuse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:46.880
and guarantee its destruction. To raise the stakes&nbsp;
even further, the machines invade Zion and kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:51.920
every free human, meaning the death of the&nbsp;
Matrix would be equivalent to human extinction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.600
This leaves the One no choice but to cooperate.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.960
The machines allow the One to free a&nbsp;
handful of humans to repopulate Zion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:06.160
and form a new Resistance. These humans&nbsp;
operate under the false belief they were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:11.120
the first to escape from the Matrix.&nbsp;
The Oracle guides this new generation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:17.520
telling them the One will be reborn to save the&nbsp;
rest of humanity. When they find the next One,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.640
they bring him to the Oracle, and the&nbsp;
cycle continues, over and over again.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:25.520
"No way! No way, this is crazy."

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:31.200
During the sixth cycle of the Matrix,&nbsp;
something changes that allows Oracle to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:36.000
help break the cycle and bring an actual end&nbsp;
to humanity's enslavement by the machines.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:40.720
It's possible that she's tried to corrupt&nbsp;
the Architect's system before — after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.640
she claims that her role is&nbsp;
to "unbalance" the Matrix .

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:48.960
This time, the Oracle is able to influence&nbsp;
humans to make a different outcome possible.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.560
The future is created by the choices of&nbsp;
individuals and, as she says, no one can see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.560 --> 00:04:01.440
past a choice they don't understand. The Oracle&nbsp;
understands more than most, but not everything.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:04.400
In a cut scene of the video game Enter the Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:10.320
the Oracle says "the path of the One is made by&nbsp;
many" and that everyone has their role to play,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:15.200
including herself. The Oracle isn't certain&nbsp;
her plan will work, even in the very end.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.120
Like everyone else, she's forced to act on faith&nbsp;
that a peaceful end to the war is possible.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.960
By the sixth incarnation, it becomes commonplace&nbsp;
for members of the Resistance to visit the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:32.640
Oracle to ask her about their purpose. When young&nbsp;
Morpheus seeks the Oracle's counsel, she tells him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:39.440
he's destined to find the One. Morpheus scours the&nbsp;
Matrix for signs of the One with great confidence.

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:45.920
The Oracle tells Trinity, a member of Morpheus'&nbsp;
crew, that she'll fall in love with a man and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:51.760
that he would be the One. Trinity reveals this&nbsp;
to her cynical shipmate, Cypher. When Morpheus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:57.840
identifies the hacker Neo as potentially being the&nbsp;
One, Cypher ridicules Trinity about her feelings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:04.320
as she is indecisive. Trinity does indeed fall&nbsp;
for Neo but decides to keep this to herself.

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:10.240
After training him on how to survive in the&nbsp;
Matrix, Morpheus takes Neo to meet the Oracle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:16.480
for the first time. Morpheus believes that Neo&nbsp;
is the One and that the Oracle will confirm this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.480 --> 00:05:21.440
but Neo isn't so sure. Neo speaks with&nbsp;
the Oracle privately about his doubts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:28.880
Above the entrance to her kitchen reads the Latin&nbsp;
phrase "temet nosce", which means "know thyself."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.880 --> 00:05:33.600
The Oracle tells Neo he's not the&nbsp;
One unless he knows he's the One — he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.200
doesn't believe this about himself,&nbsp;
so he assumes that he isn't the One.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:42.080
The Oracle lets Neo run with that assumption.&nbsp;
She also tells him that Morpheus will attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:46.640
to sacrifice himself and that Neo can save&nbsp;
him, but only at the cost of his own life.

00:05:47.280 --> 00:05:51.840
When exiting the Matrix, Morpheus and his&nbsp;
crew are betrayed by Cypher, and Morpheus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:57.760
throws himself at the machine's Agent enforcers to&nbsp;
buy Neo time to escape. However, Neo and Trinity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:03.280
go back and rescue him and Neo is killed in&nbsp;
the attempt, just as the Oracle predicted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:08.720
but revived shortly thereafter. Trinity&nbsp;
admits she loves Neo, and therefore he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:15.040
is the One. Trinity's belief revives Neo, and&nbsp;
the entire party escapes back to the real world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:20.400
Neo and Trinity build a romantic bond that&nbsp;
becomes key to the future of humanity.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:25.040
The next time Neo goes to visit&nbsp;
the Oracle in The Matrix Reloaded,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:29.520
he's confronted by her bodyguard,&nbsp;
Seraph. Seraph is also a program,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:34.560
possibly as old as the Oracle herself. Those&nbsp;
who seek a consultation with the Oracle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:39.280
must first fight Seraph, not to defeat&nbsp;
him, but to demonstrate their skills.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:43.920
In the case of Neo, Seraph tests him to&nbsp;
determine whether or not he is truly the One.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:49.760
Seraph says that "you do not truly know someone&nbsp;
until you fight them," and while this might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:54.320
just seem like an excuse for a movie to add&nbsp;
an extra fight scene, it's also clever that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:59.520
a program like the Oracle would restrict access&nbsp;
via the martial arts equivalent of a login page.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:04.320
However, Seraph can also allow people&nbsp;
other than the One to visit the Oracle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:09.760
In Enter the Matrix, Seraph submits other&nbsp;
Resistance fighters to the same test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:13.600
and they are each admitted to see&nbsp;
her as well. If someone demonstrates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:17.600
that they're dedicated enough, they can&nbsp;
earn the right to speak to the Oracle.

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:23.840
When Neo visits the Oracle in The Matrix Reloaded,&nbsp;
he arrives with a much greater understanding of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:29.520
the Matrix and is able to deduce that Seraph&nbsp;
and the Oracle are programs, rather than humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:35.520
with special abilities. The Oracle implies she&nbsp;
is an exile, hiding so she won't be deleted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:40.400
but this might not be true — while she operates&nbsp;
autonomously inside the Matrix, she's still a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.920
part of the machines' system of control, since&nbsp;
the cycle of the One depends on her cooperation.

00:07:45.920 --> 00:07:49.280
And so, the Oracle instructs&nbsp;
Neo on how to reach the Source,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.640
telling him this is, quote,&nbsp;
"where the path of the One ends."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:57.840
The Oracle doesn't lie to Neo; she only&nbsp;
gives exactly the information necessary.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:03.920
Neo follows her advice and encounters the&nbsp;
Architect, learning the truth about the prophecy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:10.240
of the One and the Oracle's role in creating the&nbsp;
Matrix. Unlike his predecessors, Neo refuses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:15.440
participate in rebooting the Matrix since it&nbsp;
means the death of his true love, Trinity.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:20.400
This is the Oracle's design — by pairing&nbsp;
Neo and Trinity, she gives the One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:26.320
something beyond human survival to fight for.&nbsp;
He chooses to break the cycle to save Trinity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:29.440
ensuring the Machine War ends, one way or another.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.960
"I knew it, he's the one."

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:37.680
The Oracle is played by two different&nbsp;
actors in The Matrix Reloaded,The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:42.480
Matrix Revolutions, and the game&nbsp;
Enter the Matrix. The original Oracle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:47.200
Gloria Foster passed away before her scenes&nbsp;
for the rest of the series could be completed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:54.000
She was succeeded by Mary Alice, who co-starred&nbsp;
as her sister in the play Having Our Say.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:58.400
The Matrix Revolutions acknowledges the&nbsp;
casting change and provides an in-universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:03.200
explanation for the Oracle's new appearance&nbsp;
that is fleshed out in Enter the Matrix.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:09.520
In the game, the Oracle explains that her&nbsp;
choice to help Neo has enraged the Merovingian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:13.680
a powerful exiled program and the&nbsp;
secondary antagonist of the trilogy.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:18.880
Among the Merovingian's interests is arranging&nbsp;
for programs that have fallen out of favor with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:24.480
the Machine World to hide out inside the&nbsp;
Matrix. He agrees to help the young program&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.880
Sati reach the Matrix only if her&nbsp;
parents, Kamala and Rama Kandra,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:33.680
deliver him a termination code that can destroy&nbsp;
the Oracle's preferred physical appearance.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:40.240
This is mostly an act of spite, but the loss of&nbsp;
her old body does seem to weigh upon The Oracle.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:47.040
Neo and the Oracle meet again in The Matrix&nbsp;
Revolutions. Neo asks the Oracle why she hid so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:52.160
much of the truth from him, and the Oracle&nbsp;
replies "it wasn't time". On this visit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:58.000
Neo's has specific questions, and the Oracle has&nbsp;
direct answers. The Oracle wants the war to end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:02.400
and she's been working toward this goal for&nbsp;
a long time. Now, it's within reach and will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:08.160
require the One to travel to the Source in the&nbsp;
real world. The Oracle isn't certain about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:13.680
details — everything that's happening now is new,&nbsp;
off-track from the repeating course of history,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:18.400
and clouded by a series of choices that&nbsp;
neither she nor Neo can understand.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:24.400
Another unexpected element is the malevolent&nbsp;
program called Smith. Originally assigned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:29.840
to protect the status quo of the Matrix, Smith&nbsp;
has gone rogue and presents a threat to humans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:35.440
and machines. Smith has gained the ability to&nbsp;
rewrite other programs and human avatars, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:42.080
is slowly taking over the entire simulation. The&nbsp;
machine has no control, and Neo is the only force&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:48.080
powerful enough to stop him. Smith assimilates the&nbsp;
Oracle, which grants him her powers of foresight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:53.360
However, like the Oracle, he can't see&nbsp;
past a choice he doesn't understand.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:57.840
At the Oracle's request, Neo&nbsp;
journeys to the Machine City,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:02.400
where the mainframe of the Matrix lives and&nbsp;
programs are born. The machines are poised to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:07.120
wipe out all of humanity but are in danger&nbsp;
from Smith, who has conquered the Matrix.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:11.440
Neo offers to go back into the&nbsp;
Matrix and defeat Smith. In exchange,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:17.920
the machines must spare Zion and allow the human&nbsp;
minds in the Matrix to escape if they choose.

00:11:17.920 --> 00:11:23.040
The machines accept Neo's terms and he battles&nbsp;
with Smith, who has foreseen his own victory.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:28.560
Smith finds himself standing over a battered&nbsp;
Neo, ready to deliver the killing blow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.000
when he becomes flustered. He finds himself&nbsp;
repeating a phrase the Oracle once spoke to Neo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:40.400
"Everything that has a beginning has an end."&nbsp;
This final message from the Oracle helps Neo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:45.520
understand the choice he needs to make:&nbsp;
sacrifice himself to defeat the enemy. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:51.120
allows Smith to overwrite his code, which gives&nbsp;
the machines a way to burn out the Smith virus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:56.160
Smith can't understand this choice&nbsp;
and therefore walks into his own doom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.160 --> 00:12:01.200
Smith is destroyed, and everything he&nbsp;
re-coded is restored — including the Oracle.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:08.080
The final scene of the original Matrix trilogy&nbsp;
sees the Oracle meet with the Architect to discuss&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:14.240
the future of the Matrix. The Architect tells&nbsp;
the Oracle she's, quote, "played a very dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:19.520
game," confirming that, from his view, she's&nbsp;
been the mastermind behind the entire revolution.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:25.440
If the Architect can be taken at his word, the&nbsp;
next incarnation of the Matrix will allow for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:30.720
humans to choose to accept the simulation,&nbsp;
and whether or not to remain there. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:35.840
change has been the Oracle's goal all along,&nbsp;
a hard-won victory in a centuries-long chess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:40.960
match against the Architect. She may not have&nbsp;
known for certain her plan would succeed, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.960 --> 00:12:46.480
like everything else in The Matrix, her victory&nbsp;
hinged on her belief in the cause and in Neo.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:53.040
This newfound peace can't be sustained forever,&nbsp;
as unrest would eventually return to the Matrix,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:59.440
both in the video game sequel The Matrix Online&nbsp;
and The Matrix Resurrections. What role the Oracle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:04.960
will play in the future remains to be seen, hidden&nbsp;
by narrative choices we don't yet understand.

